WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.860
One of the things I've been talking about
during the last year of Donald Trump's presidency

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:12.170
and during the campaign and during the transition
period and during Joe Biden's nascent presidency,

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:17.570
is that the Republican Party at this point
has stopped even pretending to be about policy

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:26.249
and values and is merely about performative
outrage, misplaced outrage, laughable outrage.

00:00:26.249 --> 00:00:28.419
We're going to look at an example in a moment.

00:00:28.419 --> 00:00:30.829
But I think this is an important sort of reset
to do.

00:00:30.829 --> 00:00:34.469
And I know many of you might be thinking,
David, you know, the Republican Party hasn't

00:00:34.469 --> 00:00:37.190
really been about policy for a very long time.

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:38.190
That's true.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:40.540
But they used to pretend to be about policy
for a time.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:46.170
The Republican Party really was about tax
cuts for the rich, cutting budgets by cutting

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:52.360
social programs, spreading, spreading the,
quote, spreading democracy through invasive

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:54.589
foreign policy around the world.

00:00:54.589 --> 00:01:00.179
They tried passing bills to get these things
done eventually during the end of the Bush

00:01:00.179 --> 00:01:05.370
era and into the Barack Obama presidency,
both terms, the Republican Party started to

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:10.070
become about policy in name only, but not
sincerely.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:14.080
They went from really trying to do policy
to just talking about it, but not really caring

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:15.080
about policy.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:19.050
You know, they'd claim to be about cutting
the deficit and reducing the debt and fiscal

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:23.730
responsibility, but not when George W. Bush
wanted to explode the deficit by going to

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:26.390
war with the wrong country.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:30.570
And they refused to acknowledge when Barack
Obama did cut the deficit.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:36.640
So they went from being about a few policies,
bad policies, policies I disagreed with to

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:41.270
only claiming to be about those policies while
not actually doing a thing about it.

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:46.960
And we saw more and more that the Republican
Party became obsessed with grievances.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:48.780
The so-called war on Christmas.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:53.970
They were fighting, fighting, non-existent
censorship, fighting nonexistent oppression

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:59.550
by gay people at what they called the gay
lobby rather than of LGBTQ folks, that type

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:00.760
of thing.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:07.070
And then Trump ran on policy, terrible policy,
but he ran on it and then just didn't do it.

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:10.440
When he became president of the United States,
he ran on building a wall.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:11.570
He didn't build it.

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:15.430
He ran on replacing Obamacare with a beautiful
new health care plan.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:16.430
Plan never existed.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:20.030
I think we're still two weeks away from Trump
unveiling it, even though he's out of office.

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:22.660
He ran on paying off the debt in one term.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:24.050
He did the opposite.

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:29.360
And over the presidency of Donald Trump, the
Republican Party went from being about these

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.120
bad policy ideas to being about the news.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.540
This fake, you can only trust us.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:37.270
Everybody else is lying to you.

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:40.890
Democrats are censoring you and social media
censoring you.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:43.230
And they're being unfair to Trump.

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:44.310
They're canceling Thanksgiving.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:45.310
They're canceling Christmas.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:47.150
They're canceling the Constitution.

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:50.860
They're canceling, you know, covid guidelines
violate the Constitution.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:57.550
And so what we have left today is a Trump
in Republican Party that is about nothing

00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:00.030
other than performative outrage.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:03.110
What policy is Marjorie Taylor Greene about?

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:04.110
Nothing.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:08.600
She barely even pretends to be about policy
because she knows nothing about policy and

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.100
it's essentially a grievance campaign.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:13.580
What policy is Madison Cawthorn about?

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:14.580
Nothing.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:18.670
And in fact, we've gotten reports from inside
his staff that he is running a communications

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:21.930
platform rather than a policy platform.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:26.920
We know we could tell it's all about being
outraged at the left for things that don't

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:27.930
even exist.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:31.950
And right wing media has jumped on the train,
probably because it's profitable for them.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:34.720
I'm going to play a clip now that is the epitome
of this.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:40.150
Fox News invited a Minnesota Republican state
senator named Julia Coleman on.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:41.720
Why did they do that?

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.620
Because she's furious.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.569
And Fox News is outraged that.

00:03:45.569 --> 00:03:53.660
Minnesota educational standards don't rail
against socialism enough, and that's the reason

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:54.770
that she's outraged.

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:55.940
Take a look.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:04:00.520
Standards have a stated purpose, more like
that of the 16 19 project than that of maintaining

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:01.520
freedom.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:06.150
Well, that it's all part of an evolution that
went from the civics department to social

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:07.150
studies.

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:08.150
Here's here's a reality.

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:10.871
We actually reached out to the Minnesota Department
of Education for a statement.

00:04:10.871 --> 00:04:12.390
Here's a portion of what they said.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:17.409
They said, The benchmarks listed in this first
draft are simply examples of what could be

00:04:17.409 --> 00:04:21.719
included under each standard historical US
events like World War Two and the Holocaust

00:04:21.719 --> 00:04:23.490
are being taught in Minnesota schools.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:28.029
We welcome Senator Coleman's feedback as we
as well as the feedback of every American.

00:04:28.029 --> 00:04:33.789
So based on what you've revealed, do you feel
like they're fairly including portions of,

00:04:33.789 --> 00:04:34.789
say, World War Two?

00:04:34.789 --> 00:04:38.870
And would they exclude them if no one spoke
up about it?

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:41.729
If you didn't expose this, what would they
get away with?

00:04:41.729 --> 00:04:47.389
Well, quite frankly, this is not exactly true
what they're saying, because five thousand

00:04:47.389 --> 00:04:52.330
parents in Minnesota reached out to the review
board stating their concerns and they were

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:54.499
brushed off in a recent meeting.

00:04:54.499 --> 00:04:59.389
Now, if you're having trouble understanding
what she's so mad about and what Fox host

00:04:59.389 --> 00:05:05.729
Pete Hegseth is so mad about, it's because
it's all a performative farce.

00:05:05.729 --> 00:05:11.940
This is what the Republican Party in the immediate
post Trump era is about nothing, outrage,

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:13.889
porn based on nothing.

00:05:13.889 --> 00:05:19.759
Now, the question becomes and it's a it's
an important question for the Republican Party

00:05:19.759 --> 00:05:25.270
to answer, how long can the Republican Party
survive on the platform of baseless outrage?

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:29.150
For a while it will work because you're getting
people outraged.

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:34.400
But if they continue to be about imaginary
censorship while voting against the covid

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:39.759
relief bill that Joe Biden and Democrats get
done and it gets money to people and voters

00:05:39.759 --> 00:05:46.839
know it, what is this outrage, performative
nonsense do for them in the twenty two midterms?

00:05:46.839 --> 00:05:52.540
I don't know the answer and it remains to
be seen, but it could be very, very bad.

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:57.650
And we'll talk about it a little bit more
later in the context of this third party that

00:05:57.650 --> 00:06:03.069
Donald Trump is looking at and which 64 percent
of Republicans, if you can believe it, would

00:06:03.069 --> 00:06:06.880
be open to joining and abandoning the Republican
Party.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.349
We'll talk about that later.

00:06:08.349 --> 00:06:11.039
You can find me on Twitter at David Pakman,

